implementationPlan.description:
TESTS FIRST (RED). Create packages/moe-daemon/src/state/dependencyReadiness.strict.test.ts.

CONTRACT (re-plan of the blocked rev 1). A STRICT consumer is decided exactly as CQ-M01c/e/f decide strictness: `resolveTaskExecutionProfile(settings, consumer.executionPolicySnapshot) === 'verified-local'`, i.e. the live profile floored by the consumer's stored verified-local snapshot.
- Every legacy/observe consumer keeps today's rule, whatever the live deliveryPolicy. M01f's executionPolicyIntegration E1-control pins this: a legacy-captured prerequisite under live observe/local-branch releases its waiter.
- A prerequisite is LEGACY when its OWN captured snapshot is not verified-local: readExecutionPolicySnapshot(dep.executionPolicySnapshot)?.profile is absent, v1 legacy/observe, or v2 legacy/observe. That identity is used only to refuse, never to grant.
- resolveTaskDeliveryPolicy and evaluateDeliveryEvidence are NOT changed.

FIXTURE. Copy (never import a .test.ts) the proven helpers of delivery/requiredChecks.strong.test.ts:
- the `vi.mock('../delivery/executionProfile.js', ...)` that makes assertExecutionProfileReady a no-op in THIS file only, plus one row pinning that the real assertion still throws;
- settings/profile/approve/candidate/dispatch/observe/pass and a setDone that stores qa_approve's record: an 'approve' Review on the current candidate (h.state.reviews.set).

The architect probe P1-P7 ran on exactly these helpers at 87a1e939 and passed. A prerequisite planned through submit_plan under live verified-local captures a v2 verified-local snapshot. Seed consumers as raw rows with an explicit snapshot: STRICT = v2 {profile 'verified-local', deliveryPolicy 'local-branch'}; LEGACY = none or v2 observe. Flip the live profile to 'observe' for legacy-consumer rows. Assert exact literal tokens and exact unmet lists, table-driven (it.each).

DoD1, strict consumer. Each of these is unmet with exactly these tokens:
- a DONE prerequisite with complete evidence AND an approval, but a captured observe or legacy (or absent) profile: ['verified-local-snapshot'];
- an id never on the board: ['prerequisite-missing'];
- a prerequisite removed by moe.delete_task: ['prerequisite-missing'];
- a strict DONE prerequisite flipped to DONE with no Review: ['approved-review'];
- an ARCHIVED one without retained proof: includes 'delivery-receipt';
- a non-DONE status: [].
The SAME prerequisites under a LEGACY consumer give today's answers: missing satisfied, ARCHIVED satisfied, legacy-DONE judged by evaluateDeliveryEvidence alone. Also check that the consumer-less calls stay byte-identical.

DoD2. An ARCHIVED prerequisite with all four parts of retained proof satisfies a strict consumer: a captured verified-local snapshot, evaluateDeliveryEvidence satisfied, the LAST review on its CURRENT candidate (listCandidatesForTask(...).at(-1)) being 'approve', and a delivery receipt for that candidate. One row per removed part, each with its exact token:
- no receipt: delivery-receipt;
- a receipt or an approval on an OLDER candidate only: delivery-receipt / approved-review;
- a later 'reject' on the current candidate: approved-review;
- a captured observe snapshot: verified-local-snapshot;
- a missing required pass: required-check:... from evaluateDeliveryEvidence.
A strict DONE prerequisite with an approval plus evidence also satisfies.

DoD3:
- moe.set_task_dependencies by a worker-team seat: NOT_ALLOWED, and nothing written (task file bytes unchanged).
- By an architect (removeDependsOn of the missing id):
  - the TASK_DEPENDENCIES_SET activity entry (after flushActivityLog) has workerId = that architect;
  - the task's system message contains `-[<id>]`;
  - the strict consumer's unmet list loses only that id;
  - h.state.reviews/receipts/candidates/checkRuns sizes are unchanged;
  - the consumer's own evaluateDeliveryEvidence result is deep-equal before and after;
  - a removed legacy-DONE prerequisite's strict shortfall is unchanged.
- delete_task of a prerequisite never satisfies a strict consumer.

PATHS (strict consumer; legacy control where cheap):
- runDependencyUnblock keeps a BLOCKED strict consumer on a legacy-DONE prerequisite, and restores it once the prerequisite has verified delivery;
- report_blocked with blockedOnTaskIds naming a legacy-DONE id answers not-satisfied and blocks;
- an explicit claim_next_task of a WORKING strict consumer behind a strict DONE prerequisite lacking an approval refuses DEPENDENCY_EVIDENCE_MISSING with missingEvidence ['approved-review'], and nothing is written;
- describeUnmetDependency(state, id, consumer) renders `<id> [<status|missing>, missing <tokens>]`.

Run `npx vitest run src/state/dependencyReadiness.strict.test.ts` at HEAD and record it in the step note. The strict rows and the DoD3 actor row fail by assertion (HEAD ignores a third argument). The legacy rows pass. A harness or import error is not RED. Keep the file at about 300 lines or less.

THE PREDICATE: ONE shared predicate, consumer-aware. Edit packages/moe-daemon/src/delivery/policy.ts and packages/moe-daemon/src/state/dependencyUnblock.ts.

(1) policy.ts, vocabulary only. Add to EVIDENCE_TOKENS:
- prerequisiteMissing 'prerequisite-missing'
- verifiedLocalSnapshot 'verified-local-snapshot'
- approvedReview 'approved-review'
- deliveryReceipt 'delivery-receipt'
Give each a TOKEN_REASONS entry, so describeMissingEvidence never answers 'unrecognised evidence token':
- missing: not on the board, can never prove delivery; an architect/governor removes it with moe.set_task_dependencies;
- snapshot: its own execution-policy snapshot did not capture verified-local, so it was delivered under legacy rules;
- review: no qa_approve stands on its current candidate (the last review there is not an approval, or there is no candidate);
- receipt: ARCHIVED with no delivery receipt for its current candidate.
Do NOT touch resolveTaskDeliveryPolicy, evaluateDeliveryEvidence or any other selector: CQ-M01f's Q5/E rows pin them.

(2) dependencyUnblock.ts. New imports:
- readExecutionPolicySnapshot and resolveTaskExecutionProfile from ../delivery/executionProfile.js (the leaf);
- listCandidatesForTask, listReviewsForTask, getDeliveryReceiptForCandidate from the stores;
- EVIDENCE_TOKENS from policy.ts.
All of these are already in policy.ts's runtime closure, so no new cycle.

Export the type `DependencyConsumer = Pick<Task, 'executionPolicySnapshot'>`. Add private `isStrictConsumer(state, consumer)`: consumer !== undefined && resolveTaskExecutionProfile(state.project?.settings, consumer.executionPolicySnapshot) === 'verified-local'.

private strictShortfall(state, taskId):
- missing -> {false, ['prerequisite-missing']};
- status not DONE/ARCHIVED -> {false, []};
- else collect, in this order:
  - 'verified-local-snapshot' unless readExecutionPolicySnapshot(dep.executionPolicySnapshot)?.profile === 'verified-local';
  - 'approved-review' unless the LAST review (listReviewsForTask order) whose candidateId is the current candidate (listCandidatesForTask(...).at(-1)) has decision 'approve';
  - for ARCHIVED, 'delivery-receipt' unless getDeliveryReceiptForCandidate(current) is non-null;
  - then ...evaluateDeliveryEvidence(state, dep).missingEvidence.
  satisfied iff the list is empty.

Signatures:
- dependencyShortfall(state, taskId, consumer?) and isDependencySatisfied(state, taskId, consumer?): with no consumer or a non-strict one, the existing body runs BYTE-identical.
- unmetDependsOn / unmetBlockedOnTaskIds pass their own task as the consumer (widen the Pick types with 'executionPolicySnapshot'; carriedBlockQuestion's Pick too).
- describeUnmetDependency(state, id, consumer?): legacy output word for word. For a strict consumer, render missing, DONE and ARCHIVED ids as `<id> [<status|missing>, missing <tokens>]`.
- alertStaleBlocks passes `task` to describeUnmetDependency.
- findDependencyPath stays unchanged: edges out of DONE/ARCHIVED rows gate nothing, pinned by 'cycle detection ignores delivery evidence'.

Error handling (fail closed): a malformed consumer or prerequisite snapshot, a malformed live executionProfile, NOT_READY from evaluateDeliveryEvidence, or DELIVERY_RECEIPT_AMBIGUOUS each throws out of dependencyShortfall. isDependencySatisfied then answers false with the existing warn log, and describeUnmetDependency says 'could not be judged'. A row is never released on a guess.

Update the module header and the dependencyShortfall/isDependencySatisfied comments: 'gone or ARCHIVED satisfies' holds for legacy consumers only; a verified-local consumer needs retained verified delivery. The strict branch is reachable only once verified-local is certified, or under the test-only readiness mock.

Run the step-1 file (green) and the step-2 file (83/83).

VERIFY ONCE, since the shared readiness predicate changes. Run the FULL gate fresh in a Linux-native snapshot of HEAD (mem:gotcha-daemon-linux-snapshot-gate):
- `git archive HEAD` of the whole repo;
- overlay ONLY this task's 7 files;
- `npm ci` in packages/moe-daemon under `env -i HOME=$HOME PATH=$HOME/.nvm/versions/node/v24.21.0/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin` (MOE_* unset);
- `cmp` the overlay against the worktree.

GATE: `cd packages/moe-daemon && npm test` must exit 0. Its command, exit code and output tail are the complete_task evidence. Also run `npx tsc --noEmit` (exit 0), and typecheck the new test file through a scratch tsconfig ({extends ./tsconfig.json, compilerOptions {noEmit, types:[node]}, include [that file], exclude []}), since the package tsconfig excludes tests.

Expect every pre-existing test to pass unchanged, apart from step 2's fixture. Baseline at 87a1e939: 6070 passed, 20 skipped. That includes dependencyUnblock.test.ts's strict-deliveryPolicy rows, executionPolicyIntegration's CQ-M01f Q5/E rows (E1-control included), acceptance, requiredChecks.delivery and claimNextTask.contract, which proves legacy/observe consumers are untouched.

Known peer failure: at 87a1e939 src/providers/providerDescriptor.contract.test.ts fails because 447281cf (task-c4cd6dce, in REVIEW; reported to qa-952969be) changed scripts/moe-agent.ps1's codex launch to Invoke-MoeGuardedCommand. Never edit scripts or the provider descriptor for it. If it is the ONLY failure when you run, report_blocked with blockedOnTaskIds naming the row that fixes it (c4cd6dce, or its fix row), then re-run once that lands.

planningNotes.codebaseInsights:
Architect prototype in a native Linux archive of 87a1e939 (node v24.21.0, env -i):
- baseline npm test: 6070 passed, 20 skipped, plus 1 peer failure (providerDescriptor.contract, from 447281cf);
- chosen design + step-2 fixture: an identical 6070/20/1;
- tsc --noEmit exit 0;
- runtime diff about 85 changed lines (policy.ts 12, dependencyUnblock.ts 57, claimNextTask.ts 6, reportBlocked.ts 6, setTaskDependencies.ts 2); strong fixture +7.

Probe P1-P7 (strong-test helpers, readiness mocked) all passed:
- P1: strict DONE with approval and evidence satisfies;
- P2: captured observe gives ['verified-local-snapshot'];
- P3: a later reject on the current candidate gives ['approved-review'];
- P4: an approval on an older candidate gives approved-review;
- P5: ARCHIVED gives ['delivery-receipt'] until a receipt for the current candidate makes it satisfied;
- P6: missing gives ['prerequisite-missing'], and not-DONE gives [];
- P7: a legacy consumer keeps missing satisfied.

Facts:
- The current candidate is listCandidatesForTask(...).at(-1) (checkObservationStore:98, reviewBinding:84).
- listReviewsForTask sorts by createdAt then id; reviews and receipts are append-only.
- getDeliveryReceiptForCandidate throws DELIVERY_RECEIPT_AMBIGUOUS on duplicates.
- qa_approve records a Review only when a candidate binding exists; under verified-local a candidate is required.
- activityLog writes workerId = actorWorkerId.
- UPDATE_TASK's denylist blocks dependsOn edits over /ws, so set_task_dependencies is the only removal path.
- Claim admission (claimNextTask:518) runs before the dependsOn refusal (:531).
